WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Connecting Defects to the Idea of Uncertainty

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.266
Welcome back to this session on the power of measurement.

3
00:00:10.266 --> 00:00:16.399
One of the things that we are really interested in as we start to look at this relationship.

4
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.266
Y is a function of X in terms of measurement

5
00:00:20.266 --> 00:00:26.832
is our certainty and our uncertainty over Y and X.

6
00:00:26.833 --> 00:00:32.733
So, we have considerations for both Y and for X.

7
00:00:32.733 --> 00:00:36.566
Where certainty and uncertainty is concerned.

8
00:00:36.566 --> 00:00:40.699
Now let’s recognize, that what we're certain about, in this world,

9
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:47.733
plus everything we're uncertain about is equal to 100% of everything. It’s pretty simple.

10
00:00:47.733 --> 00:00:54.499
So, certainty plus uncertainty must equal 100%. Another way of expressing that,

11
00:00:54.500 --> 00:01:01.300
is that everything that we know, plus everything that is unknown

12
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:08.300
is equal to 100% of everything. That’s pretty simple.

13
00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:14.233
The universe of what is unknown, plus the universe of what is known

14
00:01:14.233 --> 00:01:18.633
is 100% of everything. That's the total universe.

15
00:01:18.633 --> 00:01:25.633
Now another way to look at this idea, is to say that

16
00:01:25.633 --> 00:01:30.799
all of our beliefs

17
00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:37.833
plus all of our disbeliefs is 100%

18
00:01:37.833 --> 00:01:41.166
of everything.

19
00:01:41.166 --> 00:01:47.799
Now, here's another way of looking at it. Our confidence

20
00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:54.833
plus our risk is equal to a hundred percent.  See, that's another way of looking at it.

21
00:01:54.833 --> 00:01:58.299
Everything in this world we’re confident about, and everything else

22
00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:01.733
that we believe that there is risk in. Is pretty much everything.

23
00:02:01.733 --> 00:02:04.899
Here’s yet another way to look at this concept.

24
00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:11.866
Yield plus the defect rate

25
00:02:11.866 --> 00:02:17.766
is 100% of all production.

26
00:02:17.766 --> 00:02:22.366
So, recall from an example where we looked at two operations.

27
00:02:22.366 --> 00:02:26.432
Operation one had 90%. Operation two had 80%.

28
00:02:26.433 --> 00:02:30.299
The throughput yield was 72%.

29
00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:37.266
So, 72% plus the defect rate

30
00:02:37.266 --> 00:02:43.466
of 28% has to be 100% of all units produced.

31
00:02:43.466 --> 00:02:48.499
Now, it's interesting what I'm doing here. I'm measuring things.

32
00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:53.733
These are measurements. These are assessments of process capability.

33
00:02:53.733 --> 00:02:59.066
So, yield is confidence. Yield is a belief. Yield is what is known.

34
00:02:59.066 --> 00:03:02.166
Yield is my certainty.

35
00:03:02.166 --> 00:03:07.666
So, I could say that my yield is my confidence.

36
00:03:07.666 --> 00:03:14.699
Which reflects my beliefs. Which describes everything that I know.

37
00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:19.033
And that constitutes in this world, what I’m certain about.

38
00:03:19.033 --> 00:03:24.833
On the other hand, on the flipside of that coin, I could say that my defect rate

39
00:03:24.833 --> 00:03:29.533
constitutes where I'm at risk with my customer.

40
00:03:29.533 --> 00:03:34.266
Which describes the extent of disbelief they have in me.

41
00:03:34.266 --> 00:03:40.132
Which prescribes the extent to which I am an unknown.

42
00:03:40.133 --> 00:03:45.699
Which defines my uncertainty in the marketplace.

43
00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:49.033
That's an easy way that we can kind of look at this.

44
00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:54.599
But here again, in order to make these statements, I need to quantify them.

45
00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:59.233
And measure my belief, my disbelief, my confidence, my risk,

46
00:03:59.233 --> 00:04:04.899
measure my yield, my defect rate. Isn't that interesting.

47
00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:09.366
I have to measure Y and I have to measure X,

48
00:04:09.366 --> 00:04:16.099
if I'm going to get a handle on the confidence and risk that I experience.

49
00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:19.266
Lord Kelvin was absolutely right.

50
00:04:19.266 --> 00:04:23.632
If we can't express what we know in the form of measurements.

51
00:04:23.633 --> 00:04:30.633
Then we really know very little about it. And, of course Mike Harry’s corollary to that,

52
00:04:30.633 --> 00:04:36.099
is if you don't know much about it. You can't control.

53
00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:41.000
If you can't control it, then you are at the mercy of chance.

54
00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:47.366
If you are at the mercy of chance, then your risk is uncertain.

55
00:04:47.366 --> 00:04:50.332
If your risk is uncertain,

56
00:04:50.333 --> 00:04:56.666
then how in the world are you steering the ship called your business.

57
00:04:56.666 --> 00:05:03.199
So once again, we come to understand that measurement is everything

58
00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:08.633
to defining this relationship, which is what six Sigma is all about.

59
00:05:08.633 --> 00:05:13.099
Is defining our Y’s. The critical Y’s.

60
00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:18.866
At the business level, operation, process level of an organization.

61
00:05:18.866 --> 00:05:25.832
And then prescribing the critical X’s that controls those critical Y’s.

62
00:05:25.833 --> 00:05:30.299
And measuring them to remove the risk.

63
00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:37.000
To remove the uncertainty from operation of our process. To reduce our rated defects.

64
00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:43.100
So as to improve our yield, to improve our confidence in the process.

65
00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:46.166
That's what Six Sigma is all about.

66
00:05:46.166 --> 00:05:49.899
And you can see now that Six Sigma hinges

67
00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:55.833
on two fundamentally simple but critical concepts.

68
00:05:55.833 --> 00:06:01.566
The first that Y is a function of X.

69
00:06:01.566 --> 00:06:08.566
And the second is our ability to measure Y to measure X

70
00:06:08.566 --> 00:06:15.532
so that we can establish f, the function. How the two are interrelated.

71
00:06:15.533 --> 00:06:20.533
Thank you for choosing SSMI.
